    "items": [
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "The Lord Speaks"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          1
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Then the Lord answered Job from the whirlwind. He said:"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          2
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Who is this who obscures my counsel",
          "with ignorant words?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          3
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Get ready to answer me like a man;",
          "when I question you, you will inform me."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          4
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Where were you when I established the earth?",
          "Tell me, if you have understanding."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          5
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Who fixed its dimensions? Certainly you know!",
          "Who stretched a measuring line across it?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          6
        ],
        "lines": [
          "What supports its foundations?",
          "Or who laid its cornerstone"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          7
        ],
        "lines": [
          "while the morning stars sang together",
          "and all the sons of God shouted for joy?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          8
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Who enclosed the sea behind doors",
          "when it burst from the womb,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          9
        ],
        "lines": [
          "when I made the clouds its garment",
          "and total darkness its blanket, ,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          10
        ],
        "lines": [
          "when I determined its boundaries",
          "and put its bars and doors in place,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          11
        ],
        "lines": [
          "when I declared, “You may come this far, but no farther;",
          "your proud waves stop here”?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          12
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Have you ever in your life commanded the morning",
          "or assigned the dawn its place,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          13
        ],
        "lines": [
          "so it may seize the edges of the earth",
          "and shake the wicked out of it?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          14
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The earth is changed as clay is by a seal;",
          "its hills stand out like the folds of a garment."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          15
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Light is withheld from the wicked,",
          "and the arm raised in violence is broken."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          16
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Have you traveled to the sources of the sea",
          "or walked in the depths of the oceans?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          17
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Have the gates of death been revealed to you?",
          "Have you seen the gates of deep darkness?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          18
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Have you comprehended the extent of the earth?",
          "Tell me, if you know all this."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          19
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Where is the road to the home of light?",
          "Do you know where darkness lives,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          20
        ],
        "lines": [
          "so you can lead it back to its border?",
          "Are you familiar with the paths to its home?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          21
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Don’t you know? You were already born;",
          "you have lived so long!"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          22
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Have you entered the place where the snow is stored?",
          "Or have you seen the storehouses of hail,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          23
        ],
        "lines": [
          "which I hold in reserve for times of trouble,",
          "for the day of warfare and battle?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          24
        ],
        "lines": [
          "What road leads to the place where light is dispersed?",
          "Where is the source of the east wind that spreads across the earth?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          25
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Who cuts a channel for the flooding rain",
          "or clears the way for lightning,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          26
        ],
        "lines": [
          "to bring rain on an uninhabited land,",
          "on a desert with no human life,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          27
        ],
        "lines": [
          "to satisfy the parched wasteland",
          "and cause the grass to sprout?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          28
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Does the rain have a father?",
          "Who fathered the drops of dew?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          29
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Whose womb did the ice come from?",
          "Who gave birth to the frost of heaven"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          30
        ],
        "lines": [
          "when water becomes as hard as stone,",
          "and the surface of the watery depths is frozen?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          31
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Can you fasten the chains of the Pleiades",
          "or loosen the belt of Orion?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          32
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Can you bring out the constellations in their season",
          "and lead the Bear and her cubs?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          33
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Do you know the laws of heaven?",
          "Can you impose its authority on earth?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          34
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Can you command the clouds",
          "so that a flood of water covers you?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          35
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Can you send out lightning bolts, and they go?",
          "Do they report to you, “Here we are”?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          36
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Who put wisdom in the heart",
          "or gave the mind understanding?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          37
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Who has the wisdom to number the clouds?",
          "Or who can tilt the water jars of heaven"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          38
        ],
        "lines": [
          "when the dust hardens like cast metal",
          "and the clods of dirt stick together?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          39
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Can you hunt prey for a lioness",
          "or satisfy the appetite of young lions"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          40
        ],
        "lines": [
          "when they crouch in their dens",
          "and lie in wait within their lairs?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          41
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Who provides the raven’s food",
          "when its young cry out to God",
          "and wander about for lack of food?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      }
    ]
  },
